Geany Servers Plugin
====================

Adds a "Servers" tab to the Geany message window for managing local and
systemd-managed services.

Reads servertools.conf (INI format), displays one row per configured server
with live status and ping indicators, and provides start/stop/reload/ping/log
actions — all without blocking the UI thread.

Configuration
-------------

Place servertools.conf in ~/.config/geany/servertools.conf (user defaults)
and/or <project>/config/geany/servertools.conf (project overrides).

Example:

  [servers]
  server_0=🕋 nginx
  name_0=nginx
  type_0=systemd
  changes_0=reload src/www;src/cgi

  server_1=🧱 firewall
  name_1=ufw
  type_1=systemd

Keys per server (N = index):
  server_N  — display label (emoji + name); empty string hides the row
  name_N    — service name (used with systemctl)
  type_N    — systemd (default), system, or local
  start_N   — custom start command (default: systemctl start <name>)
  stop_N    — custom stop command
  reload_N  — custom reload command
  status_N  — custom status script; exit 0 = running
  ping_N    — command to ping the service
  log_N     — path to log file (enables Logs button)
  sudo_N    — prefix to prepend for privilege escalation
  changes_N — "method path1;path2" — watch paths and run method on change
  on_open_N — action to fire when a Geany project is opened (start/stop/reload)
  on_close_N— action to fire when a Geany project is closed

Requirements
------------

  * Geany 2.1+
  * GTK 3

